00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.070 align:start position:0%
 
the retirement problem in the united  states and abroad is absolutely  atrocious simply so many people do not  have enough money to actually retire  when we look at the retirement savings  that people have around the world we  first have to look and say well what age  are people actually retiring and so  we've got a chart here that shows in the  united states the official retirement  age is 67 years old but the average  retirement age is actually 68 years old  we then look in the uk it's 65 as  official 64 and a half is the average if  we then go all the way down to japan 62  is the official retirement age but 69  almost 70 years old is the average  retirement age if we go ahead and we  look back in america at the percent of  americans who have no retirement savings  42 percent of 18 to 29 year olds have no  retirement savings they're young they  haven't started yet so they've got to  get started but if you go ahead and you  look at those over 60 years old one out  of every 10 americans have nothing saved  nothing not enough but nothing saved 1  out of 10. if you go ahead and you look  at 45 to 59 year olds almost one out of  every five americans 17 percent do not  have a single dollar saved for  retirement and then if you look from 30  to 44 one out of every four americans  has zero dollars saved for retirement  again it's not saying that they don't  have enough saved it's that they have  saved zero dollars obviously not very  good if we go ahead and we look at the  median retirement savings for americans  age 55 to 64 the numbers depending on  who you ask vary a little bit but it's  still not good if you asked the center  for retirement research in 2020 they  said that the median retirement savings  for americans between ages 55 to 64 is  120 000 across their 401k and ira if you  look at the median retirement savings by  age according to the transamerica center  for retirement services uh or studies  then you can see that that median  retirement savings is still very low  americans in their 60s 172 000 americans  in their 50s 117 000 if you go all the  way down to americans in their 20s it's  16 000  let's go to americans in the six in  their 60s 172 thousand dollars if you  simply were going to live on 45 000 a  year which for most people is much less  than in their working years 45 000 a  year means that if you retire at the age  of 62 you won't make it to your 70th  birthday without running out of money  that's how bad the situation is and so  most people do not have enough money  saved to actually retire they become  more and more dependent on social  security and other types of government  support  what we know though is that those  services already believe that they are  going to run out of money in the next 10  to 15 years and so if you're a young  person you unlikely to have very big  savings in your retirement you haven't  had a ton of time to make money spend  less than you make put some in your  retirement savings and then grow that  money but what we know is that the  wealthiest americans they have figured  it out you are financially incentivized  to put money in your retirement accounts  to grow that money and so that when you  do decide to stop working when you  decide to enjoy life and live and do  whatever you want you will have enough  money there to live for as long as you  possibly can you will not be worried  about money you will not be worried  about whether the government actually  has enough money in those social  services to pay you to live and so when  we look at the retirement accounts by  percentile of net worth what we can see  is this mean retirement account in  thousands  well  of course the bottom quartile they are  not doing very well you literally can't  see it on the chart if you then go and  you look at the top decile the 90 to 100  decile you can see that they have almost  a million dollars in retirement for  whatever comes their way and so  ultimately the gap between the 75th to  90th quartile uh or a percentile to the  90th to 100 is massive there's a  difference of between 200 000 or so and  almost a million dollars that is the  difference between those at the top and  everybody else but it is not something  where there's  game is rigged against you or there's  some sort of reason why you can't be in  the top percentile if you're a young  person the whole game the whole key to  this is to start early be aggressive and  continue to compound as much capital as  possible in those retirement accounts  you're incentivized to do it from a tax  perspective and so  rich people understand this better than  anybody the median net worth of  households with iras was nine times  higher than those that do not have one  so quite literally the people who have  an ira are nine times more likely to  make money than those without it rich  people understand that the tax  advantages of a retirement account are  there for everybody and so what are  those tax advantages and why are the  wealthy actually using this well there's  different types of tax advantages that  you can use there's different types of  iras the main two are a roth ira and a  traditional ira the traditional iras  allow you to contribute tax deduction  deductible assets so they lower your tax  burden today when you go ahead and you  contribute the government will not tax  you on the money that you're  contributing in to that traditional ira  a roth ira however allows you to make  contributions after you've paid your  taxes if you make a hundred dollars and  you pay 35 in taxes the remaining 65 you  may be able to take five dollars and put  it into the retirement you are not  getting any sort of tax break today but  you will not have to pay taxes when you  take the money plus gains out later so  one you get a tax deduction today and  you compound the money and have to pay  taxes when you withdraw the other you  pay your taxes today you take after tax  dollars you contribute it into a roth  ira and then you can compound that money  and when you take it out you pay no  taxes  i bet i know what you're thinking the  roth iras pretty damn cool and so in  both accounts you don't pay capital  gains tax if you trade within the  account you can go back and forth  between assets with no tax ramifications  and the maximum contribution for most  people is about six thousand dollars  annually and so ultimately what you want  to do is you want to max out that  concert that contribution whatever your  contribution maximum amount is you  should put that in every single year  whatever it takes get it in there and  then what you should be able to do is  think about what can you actually put  into your ira well your ira can hold all  sorts of different things especially  those roth iras you can do everything  from fire trucks and farmland also  private company equity we've talked  about people like peter thiel in the  past but you can also put bitcoin and  for most young people they do not know  this you can actually put tax advantage  dollars into a retirement account and  then you can purchase bitcoin within the  retirement account you can hold it for  very long periods of time and if you use  after tax dollars so after i pay my  taxes this year if i take some dollars  that i have left over i put it into my  roth ira i then purchase bitcoin in the  roth ira and i hold it for the next 30  years when i take it out i will not have  to pay taxes on the gains very very tax  efficient way to gain bitcoin exposure  and so when you think about this there's  a whole bunch of different ways that you  can do it i can tell you what i  personally do i use something called  choice and i've talked to these guys a  million times over there they do  everything from literally farmland and  fire trucks to allowing people to do it  with bitcoin the reason why i use choice  is because they allow you not only to  buy the bitcoin and have it held by a  custodian but also if you want you can  hold the private keys of the bitcoin in  your retirement account and so they have  all kinds of different options i highly  suggest if you do not have a roth ira  you should go and you should do it i  literally emailed the guys and i said  hey how the hell can you guys help  people do this and these are the three  bullet points they sent back they allow  you to hold bitcoin and other assets in  a retirement account alongside stocks  ets fire trucks farmland anything else  there's no annual fee and the only fees  you pay are when you trade about one  percent and earlier this month they  launched a referral program that pays  you and your friends to get your money  out of the legacy system in bitcoin i  don't know how the referral program  works i feel like if i'm talking about  them right now we should be getting a  referral but we're not so maybe we will  have to try to figure that out later so  the whole key to this is if you go and  you open a roth ira pay your taxes take  after tax dollars invest it in a roth  then you can buy bitcoin or other assets  you don't have to buy bitcoin you can  buy stocks or anything else and then  basically you hold those assets for long  periods of time all of the compounding  and capital gains that you get when you  take it out you won't have to pay taxes  which is like one of the greatest  arbitrages in the world in terms of  being able to actually invest and use  the tax code to your advantage

